# ---- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
**/target/
**/node_modules/
/dist/
**/*.rs.bk
.cargo
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/

# Binaries never belong in git. The few that must be (lua.dll, the
# Marianas .miz) are tracked explicitly, and a tracked file isn't affected by
# these rules.
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.so
*.dylib
*.o
*.a
*.rlib

# ---- logs and local run output -------------------------------------------------
*.log
Logs/
bfdb_log.txt
netidx_out.txt
test_stats.jsonl
*.tmp
*.orig
*.rej
/tmp/

# ---- local config and secrets -------------------------------------------------
netidx-resolver.json
bfsystem.local.ps1
# Live DCSServerBot deployment config copied from a server: real
# credentials (.secret/*.pkl tokens, postgres DSN, Discord client secret,
# CheckWX/Gemini API keys, admin_password, dashboard_secret). The committed
# plugin/extension sources and *.sample.yaml templates are the shareable half;
# this tree is not. Both spellings: the lowercase one only catches `Config/` on
# case-insensitive filesystems.
DCSServerBot/config/
DCSServerBot/Config/
Server Bot/
# Real plugin configs, wherever a copy of a bot's plugins/ folder lands.
**/plugins/fowlengine/fowlengine.yaml
**/plugins/smartmod/smartmod.yaml
**/plugins/*.zip
# Packaged extension bundle -- rebuilt from DCSServerBot/extensions/
DCSServerBot/extensions.zip
# Signing keys and certificates (deploy/signing-keys.md). The public halves
# are *.pub and stay committable.
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
# Bot backups (deploy/backups/) and Fowl Engine Manager backup zips
*.fowlbak
FowlEngine-backup-*.zip
# Dated config backups taken before a live edit -- local only
miz/ODFv2_CFG.bak-*
# Fowl Engine plugin build stamp -- written into an installed plugin by the
# updater / Fowl Engine Manager, never part of the source tree
.fowl-plugin.json

# ---- generated docs and data --------------------------------------------------
# Generated rustdoc for dcso3 -- see https://docs.rs/dcso3, or run
# `cargo doc -p dcso3` locally
docs/dcso3/
# Built range missions (bfrange/mission/build_range_miz.py). The Marianas one
# stays tracked: bfmanager's `tauri build` (scripts/stage-range.mjs) bundles it
# straight from the checkout.
bfrange/mission/dist/*.miz
!bfrange/mission/dist/VS_Range_Marianas.miz

# ---- editors and local tooling ------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*
\#*\#
.DS_Store
.idea
*.iml
.vscode/
.claude/
.project
.settings/
# Local audit reports and research scratch -- not part of the source tree
reports/
research_notes/
